IMPORT prelude

-- Land Tax Assessment Act 2002 (Western Australia), read with the Land Tax Act 2002 (WA) -- the home owner, and the owner
-- of other land: do I pay land tax on my home, on what date is it fixed, am I the one liable, and on other land how much.
--
-- SEAT: the home owner (and the owner of other land) -- the individual whose land is assessed. Every exported question is
-- phrased as that owner would ask it: "Is my home exempt?", "Am I liable?", "How much land tax must I pay?". The
-- Commissioner's assessments, grants and reassessments are encoded only as what they mean for the owner.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 5 (taxable land); s 6(1) (due on the 49th day after the assessment notice); s 7(1), (4) (the owner
-- at midnight on 30 June in the previous financial year is liable; joint owners jointly and severally); s 8(3) (agreement
-- for sale: the vendor until the purchaser obtains possession); s 9A (report errors in the notice; $5 000); s 10 (rate
-- times taxable value); s 11(1) (aggregation of all one person's taxable land); s 12(1), (3) (joint land assessed as if one
-- owner, separately); s 17 and s 18 (whole and partial exemption); s 20(3)-(5) (appeal to the Minister, 60 days, tax still
-- payable); s 20A(4) (latest date the owner can be made to report an event); s 21 (the private residence exemption); s 23
-- (one more year after the resident owner's death); s 24 and s 24A (construction of a home, 1 and 2 year exemptions);
-- s 26A (home of a disabled relative); s 26B (owner in full-time care); s 27 (moving between 2 homes); s 40 (war widow or
-- widower, first $10 000); Glossary clause 1 ("private residence", "private residential property", "primary residence",
-- "commencement date", "completion date", "owner") and clause 6 (taxable value: the lesser of capped and unimproved value);
-- Land Tax Act 2002 s 5, Table 11 (rates for 2015/16 and subsequent financial years), as a table.
--
-- Edition: compilation of the Land Tax Assessment Act 2002 (No. 52 of 2002) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49123.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 49123, retrieved 2026-09-07); no compilation
-- number or date stated; the compilation includes the Land Tax Assessment Amendment (Build-to-Rent) Act 2026 (No. 6 of 2026).
-- Rates: the Land Tax Act 2002 (No. 51 of 2002) as deposited at
-- ../../../land-tax-act-2002/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_28122.txt (mrdoc 28122, retrieved 2026-09-07), compilation table
-- ending with the Land Tax Amendment Act 2015 (No. 24 of 2015). The "prescribed percentage" for the capped value (Glossary
-- clause 6(4)) is set by regulations that are NOT deposited: it is an INPUT.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the newly subdivided land rules (ss 14, 15, 15A, 15B, 43A, Subdivision 2 of Part 3 Division 2); non-strata
-- home units (s 16); s 13; the Commissioner's discretionary grants (s 20(1)-(2A)); the executor exemptions for a life
-- tenant or future owner (ss 22, 23A); refurbishment (ss 25, 25A); construction or refurbishment of a second home (s 27A);
-- the 2020-2023 construction stimulus (ss 28F-28K: commencement 1 July 2020 to 30 June 2023 only); the trust for a disabled
-- beneficiary (s 26) except that trust property is excluded from s 21; the inner city rebate (s 28); primary production
-- (Part 3 Division 3); Crown, charitable, religious, retirement, park and build-to-rent land (Divisions 4 to 4B); ss 41,
-- 42A, 42, 43B; s 45A (minor interests disregarded); the Glossary clause 2(4)-(5) integration of several lots (a FACT here:
-- one case is one lot); the partial use of a home for a non-residential purpose (s 18(2)-(3), s 20(1)(a)); the rates for
-- assessment years before 2015/16 (Land Tax Act Tables 1-10); the Taxation Administration Act 2003 (objections, interest,
-- penalty tax).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the home owner, with the design defaults ruled
-- on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. A financial year is named by the calendar year in which it ENDS: 2029/30 is 2030. A day is written as the
-- number YYYYMMDD (15 July 2029 is 20290715). Money is in dollars.

§ `Land Tax Assessment Act 2002 -- the home owner`

§§ `Arithmetic and the calendar`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- The financial year runs from 1 July to 30 June. A day on or after 1 July falls in the year ending the next 30 June.
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year of` MEANS
    IF `the day` MINUS FLOOR (`the day` DIVIDED BY 10000) TIMES 10000 AT LEAST 701
    THEN FLOOR (`the day` DIVIDED BY 10000) PLUS 1
    ELSE FLOOR (`the day` DIVIDED BY 10000)

@export In which financial year does this day fall (named by the year in which it ends)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `In which financial year does this day fall` IS `the financial year of` `the day`

-- Glossary cl 1: "assessment year, in relation to land tax, means the financial year for which the land tax is, or is to
-- be, assessed". s 7(1): land tax for an assessment year "is payable by the person who is or was the owner of the land at
-- midnight on 30 June in the previous financial year". s 21(1) tests use and ownership at the same moment. That moment is
-- the "taxing date" in this encoding (the Act does not use the phrase).
GIVEN `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxing date for` MEANS (`the assessment year` MINUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS 630

@export At midnight on which day is my land tax for this assessment year fixed (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessment year, named by the year in which it ends (2029/30 is 2030)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `At midnight on which day is my land tax fixed` IS `the taxing date for` `the assessment year`

§§ `ss 7 and 8 -- am I the one liable?`

-- s 7(1): the owner at midnight on 30 June in the previous financial year. Glossary cl 1: "owner ... (a) in relation to land
-- ... means a person who is entitled to the land for any estate of freehold in possession".
-- s 8(3): "If an agreement has been made for the sale of land ... (a) the vendor is taken to be the owner of the land until
-- the purchaser obtains possession of the land; and (b) the purchaser is taken to become the owner of the land when the
-- purchaser obtains possession."
DECLARE `My position at the taxing date` HAS
    `I was the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was an agreement for the sale of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was the seller under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was the buyer under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buyer had obtained possession` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I liable for the land tax on this land for the assessment year (ss 7(1), 8(3))?
GIVEN `my position` IS A `My position at the taxing date` @desc Where you stood at midnight on 30 June before the assessment year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable for the land tax on this land` IF
    IF `my position`'s `there was an agreement for the sale of the land`
    THEN     (`my position`'s `I was the seller under the agreement` AND (NOT (`my position`'s `the buyer had obtained possession`)))
         OR  (`my position`'s `I was the buyer under the agreement` AND `my position`'s `the buyer had obtained possession`)
    ELSE `my position`'s `I was the owner`

-- s 7(4): "Joint owners of land are jointly and severally liable for land tax payable on the land regardless of each of
-- the joint owner's respective interests in, or use of, the land."
@export Can I be made to pay all the land tax on land I own jointly with others (s 7(4))?
GIVEN `I am a joint owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the land jointly or in common with others
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made to pay all the land tax on land I own jointly` IF `I am a joint owner`

-- s 12(3): the assessment for jointly owned land "is to be kept separate and distinct from an assessment for any land that
-- is owned -- (a) by any one of the joint owners individually".
@export Is land I own jointly assessed together with land I own alone (s 12(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my joint land assessed with my own land` IS FALSE

§§ `s 21 and the Glossary -- is my home exempt as my primary residence?`

-- Glossary cl 1: "private residence means a building or part of a building that was occupied, or fit to be occupied and
-- intended by the owner to be occupied, as a place of residence of one or more individuals, except a building or part of a
-- building that is -- (a) used as a hotel, motel, hostel, lodging house or boarding house; or (b) ordinarily used for
-- holiday accommodation" (and (c)-(f), institutional and prescribed uses, folded into the same fact).
-- "private residential property means -- (a) a lot of land on which there is a private residence".
-- "primary residence, in relation to an individual, means the individual's sole or principal place of residence" (a FACT).
--
-- s 21(1): "Private residential property (except property held in trust) is exempt for an assessment year if, at midnight
-- on 30 June in the financial year before the assessment year, it is owned -- (a) by an individual who uses it as the
-- individual's primary residence; or (b) by spouses, at least one of whom uses it as that spouse's primary residence; or
-- (c) by persons who have lived in a de facto relationship with each other for at least 2 years, whether or not they still
-- live on that basis, at least one of whom uses it as that person's primary residence."
-- s 21(2): "However, if the property is also owned by another person or persons, it is exempt if each owner who does not
-- use it for that purpose is an owner only because of a requirement by a financial institution for a guarantee of money
-- advanced on the security of the property."
DECLARE `Who owns it` IS ONE OF
    `one individual`
    `spouses`
    `de facto partners together for at least 2 years`
    `two or more other individuals`
    `a company or other body`

-- One case is one lot, at the taxing date.
DECLARE `My home at the taxing date` HAS
    `has a building occupied or fit and intended to be occupied as a residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building is a hotel, motel, hostel, lodging or boarding house or ordinarily holiday accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is held in trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owned by` IS A `Who owns it`
    `an owner uses it as their primary residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every owner who does not live there is an owner only as a guarantor a lender required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage owned by the owners who live there` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the home` IS A `My home at the taxing date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is private residential property` IF
        `the home`'s `has a building occupied or fit and intended to be occupied as a residence`
    AND (NOT (`the home`'s `the building is a hotel, motel, hostel, lodging or boarding house or ordinarily holiday accommodation`))

@export Is my land private residential property (Glossary clause 1)?
GIVEN `the home` IS A `My home at the taxing date` @desc Your home at midnight on 30 June before the assessment year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my land private residential property` IF `it is private residential property` `the home`

-- s 17(2) and s 18: an exemption applies to the whole of the lot if all its requirements apply to the whole, "otherwise,
-- only a part". s 12(2)(b): for jointly owned land the extent of an exemption takes account of "each joint owner's
-- interest in the land by virtue of which the land is exempt". INFERENCE: where co-owners who are not spouses or 2-year de
-- facto partners do not all live there and the non-residents are not mere guarantors, s 21(2) denies the whole exemption,
-- and the part exempt is the interest of the owners who live there.
DECLARE `Exemption` IS ONE OF
    `wholly exempt`
    `partly exempt`
    `not exempt`

GIVEN `the home` IS A `My home at the taxing date`
GIVETH AN `Exemption`
`the s 21 exemption for` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`it is private residential property` `the home`))
        OR `the home`'s `is held in trust`
        OR (NOT (`the home`'s `an owner uses it as their primary residence`))
    THEN `not exempt`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the home`'s `owned by`
         WHEN `one individual` THEN `wholly exempt`
         WHEN `spouses` THEN `wholly exempt`
         WHEN `de facto partners together for at least 2 years` THEN `wholly exempt`
         WHEN `two or more other individuals` THEN
             IF `the home`'s `every owner who does not live there is an owner only as a guarantor a lender required`
             THEN `wholly exempt`
             ELSE `partly exempt`
         WHEN `a company or other body` THEN `not exempt`

@export Is my home exempt from land tax as my primary residence (s 21)?
GIVEN `the home` IS A `My home at the taxing date` @desc Your home at midnight on 30 June before the assessment year
GIVETH AN `Exemption`
DECIDE `Is my home exempt as my primary residence` IS `the s 21 exemption for` `the home`

@export What percentage of my home is exempt as my primary residence (ss 21, 12(2), 18)?
GIVEN `the home` IS A `My home at the taxing date` @desc Your home at midnight on 30 June before the assessment year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What percentage of my home is exempt` IS
    CONSIDER `the s 21 exemption for` `the home`
    WHEN `wholly exempt` THEN 100
    WHEN `partly exempt` THEN `the home`'s `percentage owned by the owners who live there`
    WHEN `not exempt` THEN 0

§§ `ss 24 and 24A -- building a new home`

-- Glossary cl 1: "commencement date ... (a) if the residence is to be constructed ... under a building contract -- the date
-- when the contract is made; or (b) if ... by an owner-builder -- the date when the building permit for the work is
-- granted"; "completion date ... means the date when the construction ... is completed to the point where the residence is
-- ready for occupation". For ss 24 and 24A, private residential property includes "(d) ... a lot of land on which a private
-- residence is being or has been constructed".
--
-- s 24(1): exempt for an assessment year if "(a) the construction of the private residence ... is completed during the
-- assessment year; and (b) at midnight on 30 June in the previous financial year the individual owned the land ...; and (c)
-- the individual is the first occupant ...; and (d) the individual uses the private residence as their primary residence
-- during the assessment year." (2): not if income was derived "between the beginning of the assessment year and the time
-- when the property was first occupied", or another home of the individual is exempt for the year as their primary residence.
--
-- s 24A(1): exempt "for 2 consecutive assessment years if -- (a) the commencement date ... is -- (i) in the first assessment
-- year; or (ii) in any previous financial year and part of the construction is carried out in the first assessment year;
-- and (b) the completion date for the construction is in the second assessment year; and (c) at midnight on 30 June
-- immediately before the first assessment year, the individual owned the land ...; and (d) ... first occupant ...; and (e)
-- ... primary residence during the second assessment year." (2): the same two bars, income counted from the beginning of
-- the first assessment year.
--
-- Both sections exclude "property held in trust" and speak of property "owned by an individual". INFERENCE: spouses or
-- partners who own the land together and each meet the conditions are within them (s 12(2)(a) counts each joint owner's
-- use). INFERENCE: where the commencement date is before the first assessment year and completion falls in the second, part
-- of the construction is carried out in the first.
DECLARE `My new home being built` HAS
    `is held in trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `day I became owner of the land` IS A NUMBER
    `commencement day` IS A NUMBER
    `completion day` IS A NUMBER
    `I am the first occupant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I use it as my primary residence in the year it is completed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `income was derived from the property before I first occupied it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another home of mine is exempt as my primary residence for the year` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the build` IS A `My new home being built`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the common conditions are met` IF
        (NOT (`the build`'s `is held in trust`))
    AND `the build`'s `I am the first occupant`
    AND `the build`'s `I use it as my primary residence in the year it is completed`
    AND (NOT (`the build`'s `income was derived from the property before I first occupied it`))
    AND (NOT (`the build`'s `another home of mine is exempt as my primary residence for the year`))

GIVEN `the build` IS A `My new home being built`
      `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the one year exemption applies` IF
        `the common conditions are met` `the build`
    AND `the financial year of` (`the build`'s `completion day`) EQUALS `the assessment year`
    AND `the build`'s `day I became owner of the land` AT MOST `the taxing date for` `the assessment year`

@export Is my land exempt for this year under the one year exemption for building my home (s 24)?
GIVEN `the build` IS A `My new home being built` @desc Your new home and its construction
      `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessment year, named by the year in which it ends
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my land exempt under the one year building exemption` IF
    `the one year exemption applies` `the build` `the assessment year`

GIVEN `the build` IS A `My new home being built`
      `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the two year exemption applies` IF
        `the common conditions are met` `the build`
    AND (`the assessment year` EQUALS `first year` OR `the assessment year` EQUALS `first year` PLUS 1)
    AND `the financial year of` (`the build`'s `commencement day`) AT MOST `first year`
    AND `the build`'s `day I became owner of the land` AT MOST `the taxing date for` `first year`
    WHERE
        `first year` MEANS `the financial year of` (`the build`'s `completion day`) MINUS 1

@export Is my land exempt for this year under the two year exemption for building my home (s 24A)?
GIVEN `the build` IS A `My new home being built` @desc Your new home and its construction
      `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessment year, named by the year in which it ends
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my land exempt under the two year building exemption` IF
    `the two year exemption applies` `the build` `the assessment year`

@export Is my land exempt for this year while my new home is built (s 24 or s 24A)?
GIVEN `the build` IS A `My new home being built` @desc Your new home and its construction
      `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessment year, named by the year in which it ends
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my land exempt while my new home is built` IF
        `the one year exemption applies` `the build` `the assessment year`
    OR  `the two year exemption applies` `the build` `the assessment year`

§§ `s 27 -- moving between 2 homes`

-- s 27(1): "Private residential property (property A) is exempt for an assessment year if -- (a) at midnight on 30 June
-- in the previous financial year, the owner owned property A and another private residential property (property B); and
-- (b) property B is exempt for the assessment year because of its use by an individual at midnight on 30 June in the
-- previous financial year as the individual's primary residence; and (c) property A would have been exempt ... if ... the
-- individual had used property A as the individual's primary residence instead of property B; and (d) the property the
-- owner acquired second was acquired in the previous financial year; and (e) the individual used property A as the
-- individual's primary residence -- (i) in the previous financial year before using property B for that purpose; or (ii)
-- in the assessment year after using property B for that purpose; and (f) during the assessment year, the owner -- (i)
-- sold or otherwise disposed of the property the owner acquired first; and (ii) delivered possession of that property to
-- the new owner." (2): not exempt if, while both were owned, "the owner or any other person derived income from the
-- property that was not being used as the individual's primary residence". (3): the owner "must notify the Commissioner in
-- the approved form of when the disposal and delivery of possession of the property acquired first occurs".
DECLARE `My two homes` HAS
    `I owned both at the taxing date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the home I lived in at the taxing date is exempt for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other home would have been exempt had I lived there instead` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I acquired the second home in the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I lived in the other home before the previous one in that year or after it in the assessment year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I sold and handed over the home I acquired first during the assessment year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `income was derived from the home not lived in while I owned both` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is the home I am not living in at the taxing date exempt because I am moving between 2 homes (s 27)?
GIVEN `the homes` IS A `My two homes` @desc Your two homes around the taxing date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my other home exempt while I move` IF
        `the homes`'s `I owned both at the taxing date`
    AND `the homes`'s `the home I lived in at the taxing date is exempt for the year`
    AND `the homes`'s `the other home would have been exempt had I lived there instead`
    AND `the homes`'s `I acquired the second home in the previous financial year`
    AND `the homes`'s `I lived in the other home before the previous one in that year or after it in the assessment year`
    AND `the homes`'s `I sold and handed over the home I acquired first during the assessment year`
    AND (NOT (`the homes`'s `income was derived from the home not lived in while I owned both`))

@export Must I tell the Commissioner when I sell and hand over the home I acquired first (s 27(3))?
GIVEN `I rely on the moving exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim the s 27 exemption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commissioner when I hand over my first home` IF `I rely on the moving exemption`

§§ `s 26B -- when I am in full-time care`

-- s 26B(2): "an individual is in full-time care during any period when -- (a) the individual is being cared for by a
-- person who is qualified for a carer payment ...; or (b) the individual's primary residence is" a hospital, mental health
-- service, aged care facility, palliative care facility or the like (a FACT here).
-- s 26B(3): exempt if "(a) at midnight on 30 June in the financial year before the assessment year -- (i) the property is
-- owned by an individual as described in subsection (4); and (ii) the individual is in full-time care; and (b) immediately
-- before the care commencement date -- (i) the property was owned by the individual as described in subsection (4); and
-- (ii) the individual used the property as their primary residence." (4): owned by the individual alone, with a spouse,
-- with a 2-year de facto partner, or with guarantors only. (5): not exempt if income was derived in the relevant period, or
-- "any other property owned by the individual is exempt ... as a result of its use by the individual as their primary
-- residence". (3): "(except property held in trust)".
DECLARE `My home while I am in care` HAS
    `is held in trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owned at the taxing date by me alone, with my spouse or partner, or with guarantors only` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am in full-time care at the taxing date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `just before my care began I so owned it and lived in it as my primary residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `income was derived from it in the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another property of mine is exempt as my primary residence` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my home exempt while I am in full-time care (s 26B)?
GIVEN `the home` IS A `My home while I am in care` @desc Your former home while you are in care
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my home exempt while I am in care` IF
        (NOT (`the home`'s `is held in trust`))
    AND `the home`'s `owned at the taxing date by me alone, with my spouse or partner, or with guarantors only`
    AND `the home`'s `I am in full-time care at the taxing date`
    AND `the home`'s `just before my care began I so owned it and lived in it as my primary residence`
    AND (NOT (`the home`'s `income was derived from it in the relevant period`))
    AND (NOT (`the home`'s `another property of mine is exempt as my primary residence`))

§§ `s 26A -- a home where my disabled relative lives`

-- s 26A(2): exempt if at the taxing date "(a) a disabled person uses the property as their primary residence; and (b) it
-- is owned by one or more individuals, at least one of whom is related to the disabled person." (1): "disabled person" is
-- one qualified for the disability support pension, or a child under 16 whose carer qualifies for carer payment (FACTS
-- borrowed from the Social Security Act 1991). (3): related means "a parent or grandparent", "a brother or sister", "a
-- child", whole or half blood, natural or by written law.
@export Is my home exempt because a disabled relative of mine lives in it (s 26A)?
GIVEN `a disabled person uses it as their primary residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc A person qualified for the disability support pension (or a child under 16 whose carer qualifies for carer payment) lives there as their primary residence
      `it is owned by individuals at least one of whom is the person's parent, grandparent, sibling or child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an owner is related to that person as s 26A(3) says
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my home exempt because my disabled relative lives there` IF
        `a disabled person uses it as their primary residence`
    AND `it is owned by individuals at least one of whom is the person's parent, grandparent, sibling or child`

§§ `s 23 -- the year after I die`

-- s 23(1): property "owned by the executor or administrator of an individual's estate is exempt, but only for the
-- assessment year following the financial year in which the individual died, if -- (a) the individual's ownership and use
-- of the property as their primary residence -- (i) gave rise to an exemption under section 21 or 26B for the financial
-- year in which the individual died; or (ii) would have given rise to" one, tested immediately before death; "(b) the
-- executor or administrator is the owner of the property at midnight on 30 June in the financial year in which the
-- individual died; and (c) the individual's estate does not derive any rent or other income from the property between the
-- date of the individual's death and the end of the assessment year."
DECLARE `My home after my death` HAS
    `the financial year of my death` IS A NUMBER
    `my ownership and use gave or would have given a s 21 or s 26B exemption that year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my executor owns it at midnight on 30 June of the year of death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my estate derives rent or income from it before the end of the assessment year` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my home still exempt for my estate in this assessment year after I die (s 23)?
GIVEN `the home` IS A `My home after my death` @desc Your home in your executor's hands
      `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessment year, named by the year in which it ends
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my home exempt for my estate after my death` IF
        `the assessment year` EQUALS `the home`'s `the financial year of my death` PLUS 1
    AND `the home`'s `my ownership and use gave or would have given a s 21 or s 26B exemption that year`
    AND `the home`'s `my executor owns it at midnight on 30 June of the year of death`
    AND (NOT (`the home`'s `my estate derives rent or income from it before the end of the assessment year`))

§§ `Glossary clause 6 -- the taxable value`

-- cl 6(2): the taxable value for a financial year is "(a) if the capped value of the land can be used ..., the lesser of
-- these values at midnight on 30 June immediately before that year -- (i) the capped value of the land; (ii) the
-- unimproved value of the land; (b) otherwise, the unimproved value". (3): the capped value cannot be used for "a lot that
-- was created when land was, in the financial year immediately before that year, subdivided" (unless only for a compulsory
-- taking). (4)(b)(ii): after 2009/10 the capped value is "the prescribed percentage, for that year, of the taxable value of
-- the land for the previous financial year". The PRESCRIBED PERCENTAGE IS SET BY REGULATIONS NOT DEPOSITED: an input.
-- "unimproved value ... determined under the Valuation of Land Act 1978" is a FACT (the Valuer-General's figure).
@export What is the taxable value of my land for the year (Glossary clause 6)?
GIVEN `the unimproved value` IS A NUMBER @desc The Valuer-General's unimproved value at midnight on 30 June before the year
      `last year's taxable value` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable value of the land for the previous financial year
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage prescribed by regulations for the year (not deposited)
      `the lot was created by a subdivision last year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lot came into existence by a subdivision in the previous financial year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the taxable value of my land` IS
    IF `the lot was created by a subdivision last year`
    THEN `the unimproved value`
    ELSE `the lesser of` `the unimproved value` (`the prescribed percentage` TIMES `last year's taxable value` DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `Land Tax Act 2002 s 5, Table 11 -- the rate, as a table`

-- Land Tax Act 2002 s 5: "Land tax is imposed at the rates shown in the table to this section for the relevant financial
-- year". Table 11: "Land tax rates for 2015/16 and subsequent financial years", by "Taxable value of the land":
--   0          - 300 000       Nil
--   300 000    - 420 000       A flat rate of $300
--   420 000    - 1 000 000     $300 + 0.25 cent for each $1 in excess of $420 000
--   1 000 000  - 1 800 000     $1 750 + 0.90 cent for each $1 in excess of $1 000 000
--   1 800 000  - 5 000 000     $8 950 + 1.80 cents for each $1 in excess of $1 800 000
--   5 000 000  - 11 000 000    $66 550 + 2.00 cents for each $1 in excess of $5 000 000
--   11 000 000 -               $186 550 + 2.67 cents for each $1 in excess of $11 000 000
-- The columns are "Exceeding" and "Not exceeding": a value equal to a boundary belongs to the lower band.
DECLARE `Rate band` HAS
    `exceeding` IS A NUMBER
    `base amount` IS A NUMBER
    `cents per dollar` IS A NUMBER

-- Highest band first: the first band whose floor the value exceeds is the one that applies.
`Table 11` MEANS
    LIST `Rate band` OF 11000000, 186550, 2.67
         `Rate band` OF 5000000,  66550,  2.00
         `Rate band` OF 1800000,  8950,   1.80
         `Rate band` OF 1000000,  1750,   0.90
         `Rate band` OF 420000,   300,    0.25
         `Rate band` OF 300000,   300,    0

GIVEN `scale` IS A LIST OF `Rate band`
      `the value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on the scale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `scale`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `band` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `the value` GREATER THAN `band`'s `exceeding`
        THEN `band`'s `base amount`
             PLUS `band`'s `cents per dollar` TIMES (`the value` MINUS `band`'s `exceeding`) DIVIDED BY 100
        ELSE `the tax on the scale` `rest` `the value`

@export Does Table 11 of the Land Tax Act 2002 set the rate for this assessment year?
GIVEN `the assessment year` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessment year, named by the year in which it ends
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Table 11 set the rate for this year` IF `the assessment year` AT LEAST 2016

@export How much land tax is charged on this taxable value at the Table 11 rate (Land Tax Act 2002 s 5)?
GIVEN `the taxable value` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable value (or aggregated taxable value) of the land
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much land tax is charged on this value` IS `the tax on the scale` `Table 11` `the taxable value`

§§ `ss 10, 11, 18, 40 -- how much land tax must I pay on my land?`

-- s 10: the tax is "the amount calculated by applying the rate fixed in relation to the land under the Land Tax Act 2002
-- to the amount equal to the taxable value of the land". s 11(1): "If a person owns 2 or more lots or parcels of taxable
-- land, land tax is payable on the aggregated taxable value of all the taxable land owned by the person." Glossary:
-- "aggregated taxable value ... means the amount equal to the sum of the taxable values of each taxable lot or parcel".
-- s 18 and s 12(2): a partly exempt lot is taxed on the part not exempt.
-- s 40: land is exempt "to the extent of the first $10 000 of the value of the land on which land tax would otherwise be
-- payable" if the owner is a war widow or war widower (Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986, a FACT) or a veteran's widowed
-- mother still paid the pension.
-- s 12(3): land owned jointly is a separate assessment. One call here is one assessment: all the land I own alone, or all
-- the land owned by one set of joint owners.
DECLARE `Lot` HAS
    `taxable value` IS A NUMBER
    `percentage exempt` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `lots` IS A LIST OF `Lot`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregated taxable value of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `lots`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `lot` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        `lot`'s `taxable value` TIMES (100 MINUS `lot`'s `percentage exempt`) DIVIDED BY 100
        PLUS `the aggregated taxable value of` `rest`

@export How much land tax must I pay on all the land in this assessment (ss 10, 11, 40)?
GIVEN `my lots` IS A LIST OF `Lot` @desc Each lot in this assessment, with its taxable value and the percentage exempt
      `I am a war widow or widower, or a veteran's widowed mother on the pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 40 applies to you
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much land tax must I pay` IS
    `the tax on the scale` `Table 11`
        (`the greater of` 0 (`the aggregated taxable value of` `my lots` MINUS `the s 40 allowance`))
    WHERE
        `the s 40 allowance` MEANS
            IF `I am a war widow or widower, or a veteran's widowed mother on the pension` THEN 10000 ELSE 0

§§ `ss 6, 9A, 20, 20A -- deadlines and penalties for the owner`

-- s 6(1): "Land tax payable on an original assessment is due for payment on the 49th day after the date of the assessment
-- notice."
@export On which day after the date of my assessment notice is my land tax due (s 6(1))?
-- A reassessment is due on the date its notice specifies under the Taxation Administration Act 2003 (s 6(2)); that Act is
-- not encoded, so 0 here means "see the notice", not "due at once".
GIVEN `it is an original assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc FALSE for a reassessment, whose due date is in its notice
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `On which day after the notice is my land tax due` IS
    IF `it is an original assessment` THEN 49 ELSE 0

-- s 9A(1), (2): the person named as liable "must notify the Commissioner of any material error or omission in the notice"
-- "(a) on or before the date specified in the assessment notice as the due date ...; or (b) if no such date is specified --
-- within 21 days after the date of the assessment notice." "Penalty: $5 000." (3): a defence if the person did not know and
-- could not reasonably have known.
@export Within how many days after my assessment notice must I report an error in it (s 9A(2))?
GIVEN `the notice specifies a due date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice gives a due date for payment
      `days from the notice to that due date` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the date of the notice to the due date it gives
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I report an error in my notice` IS
    IF `the notice specifies a due date` THEN `days from the notice to that due date` ELSE 21

@export What is the most I can be fined for not reporting an error in my assessment notice (s 9A)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not reporting an error` IS 5000

-- s 20(3), (4): a taxpayer "may appeal to the Minister" against a refusal or revocation of an exemption or concession under
-- s 20(1), "within 60 days after the date on which notice of the Commissioner's decision was given". (5): "The obligation to
-- pay ... land tax, is not affected by any appeal to the Minister."
@export Within how many days may I appeal to the Minister against a refused or revoked exemption (s 20(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days may I appeal to the Minister` IS 60

@export Must I still pay the land tax while my appeal to the Minister is pending (s 20(5))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I still pay while my appeal is pending` IS TRUE

-- s 20A(4): a notice requiring the owner to report an event affecting an exemption "must not require a person to notify
-- ... (a) earlier than the 49th day after the day on which the relevant event or circumstance occurs; or (b) later than 30
-- September in the financial year after the financial year in which the relevant event or circumstance occurs." (5):
-- "Penalty for this subsection: a fine of $5 000."
@export By what day at the latest can I be required to report an event affecting my exemption (s 20A(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the day of the event` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the event happened, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By what day at the latest must I report an event affecting my exemption` IS
    `the financial year of` `the day of the event` TIMES 10000 PLUS 930
